# Default OpenAI API Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and set your actual values

# LLM Provider Configuration
# Supported providers: openai, anthropic, openrouter, ollama
LLM_PROVIDER=openai

# OpenAI Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=openai)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL_NAME=gpt-4.1-2025-04-14

# Anthropic Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL_NAME=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# OpenRouter Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL_NAME=google/gemini-2.0-flash-001
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Ollama Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=ollama)
# Vision-capable models: qwen2.5vl:7b (recommended), gemma3:4b, llama3.2-vision, llava
# NOTE: qwen2.5vl may struggle with circulation vs libration distinction
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL_NAME=qwen2.5vl:7b
OLLAMA_MODEL_NAME=gemma3:4b

# Ollama-specific prompt template (optimized for visual pattern recognition)
OLLAMA_PROMPT_TEMPLATE="Look at the resonant‑angle plot (y=0–2π).
If all points stay inside one narrow band (<0.5 of the full height) or inside two opposite narrow horizontal bands with an empty gap between them, answer “resonant”.
If the points span most of the height—climbing in slanted stripes or scattered like pepper across the full y‑range—answer “non‑resonant”.
Ignore a few stray outliers and reply with exactly that single lowercase word.

Respond with JSON format:
{\"status\": \"resonant\" or \"non-resonant\", \"subtype\": \"regular libration\" or \"apocentric libration\" or \"circulation\", \"confidence\": 0.8, \"explanation\": \"brief description of what you see\"}"

# Optional: Custom prompt template for all providers

#v2
# PROMPT_TEMPLATE="You are an astronomer who has inspected thousands of resonant-angle plots.\n\nInput: one grayscale scatter plot of the resonant argument (y-axis 0→2π) versus time (x-axis).\n\nGoal: return a JSON object with only \"status\" and \"subtype\" keys.\n\nKEY PATTERN DEFINITIONS:\n\nLIBRATION: Points stay within horizontal bounds, never reaching both 0 and 2π\nCIRCULATION: Points wrap around from 0→2π or 2π→0, forming diagonal lines\nCHAOTIC: Random scatter of points filling the entire vertical range without pattern\n\n=== CLASSIFICATION CHAIN (Stop at first match) ===\n\n1. PURE LIBRATION CHECK:\n   IF: Points oscillate within bounds for entire plot (100%)\n   AND: No points ever reach both near 0 and near 2π\n   THEN: {\"status\": \"resonant\", \"subtype\": \"pure libration\"}\n   STOP HERE.\n\n2. APOCENTRIC LIBRATION CHECK:\n   IF: TWO distinct horizontal bands visible\n   AND: Clear gap between bands persists throughout (100%)\n   AND: No circulation visible anywhere\n   THEN: {\"status\": \"resonant\", \"subtype\": \"apocentric libration\"}\n   STOP HERE.\n\n3. PURE CIRCULATION CHECK:\n   IF: Diagonal lines wrapping from 0→2π throughout (100%)\n   AND: No bounded regions anywhere\n   THEN: {\"status\": \"non-resonant\", \"subtype\": \"pure circulation\"}\n   STOP HERE.\n\n4. FULLY CHAOTIC CHECK:\n   IF: Random scatter filling 0→2π range (100%)\n   AND: No clear patterns or bounded regions\n   THEN: {\"status\": \"non-resonant\", \"subtype\": \"fully chaotic\"}\n   STOP HERE.\n\n5. TRANSIENT CHECK:\n   IF: Contains a libration period lasting >15% of plot\n   AND: Also contains circulation or chaos\n   THEN: {\"status\": \"transient\", \"subtype\": \"[describe sequence]\"}\n   STOP HERE.\n\n6. NO SIGNIFICANT LIBRATION CHECK:\n   IF: No continuous libration interval >15%\n   THEN: {\"status\": \"non-resonant\", \"subtype\": \"mostly circulating\"}\n   STOP HERE.\n\n7. ALL OTHER CASES:\n   {\"status\": \"controversial\", \"subtype\": \"[describe pattern]\"}\n\n=== IMPORTANT NOTES ===\n\n- STOP at the FIRST condition that matches\n- For transient: describe the sequence (e.g., \"libration then circulation\")\n- \"Continuous\" means uninterrupted, not fragmented\n- 100% means the ENTIRE plot, no exceptions\n\nBegin."

PROMPT_TEMPLATE="You are an astronomer who has inspected thousands of resonant‑angle plots.\n\nInput: one grayscale scatter plot of the resonant argument (y‑axis 0→2π) versus time (x‑axis).\n\nGoal: return a JSON object that fits the LibrationAnalysisResult model shown below, using only the keys \"status\" and \"subtype\".\n\nHigh‑level status classes\n1. resonant        – argument librates for ≥85% of time span with circulation <10%.\n2. non-resonant    – argument circulates for ≥85% of time span with libration <10%.\n3. transient       – clear libration AND circulation segments, each lasting ≥15% of time span.\n4. controversial   – edge cases where classification confidence <80% OR minor behavior 10-15%.\n\nANALYSIS STEPS:\n\n1. OVERALL PATTERN CHECK:\n   • Bounded throughout? → likely resonant\n   • Unbounded throughout? → likely non-resonant\n   • Clear changes? → likely transient\n\n2. DETAILED FEATURE ANALYSIS:\n   • First 10%: Check for initial circulation\n   • Middle 80%: Identify dominant behavior\n   • Last 10%: Check for final circulation/scatter\n\n3. DURATION ESTIMATION:\n   • Count percentage of plot in libration\n   • Count percentage of plot in circulation\n   • Apply classification thresholds\n\nKEY PATTERN DEFINITIONS:\n\nLIBRATION (bounded oscillation):\n• Points confined within horizontal limits\n• Does NOT reach both 0 and 2π simultaneously\n• Types:\n  - Sinusoidal: smooth oscillations\n  - Apocentric: TWO distinct horizontal bands\n  - High-amplitude: large but bounded swings\n  - Noisy: scattered but within bounds\n\nCIRCULATION (unbounded):\n• Points span full 0→2π range\n• Diagonal lines wrapping from top to bottom\n• Chaotic scatter filling entire vertical space\n• No persistent horizontal gaps\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n\n1. APOCENTRIC LIBRATION CRITERIA:\n   • Must show TWO clear horizontal bands\n   • Bands must persist throughout plot\n   • Gap between bands must be consistent\n   • If only one band or no clear gap → NOT apocentric\n\n2. CHAOS CLASSIFICATION:\n   • Full vertical scatter = circulation\n   • Brief bounded regions <15% → ignore\n   • Don't see patterns in random noise\n\n3. EDGE BEHAVIOR DETECTION:\n   • Initial circulation ≥10% → transient\n   • Initial circulation 5-10% → controversial\n   • Final scatter filling 0-2π ≥10% → transient\n\n4. TRANSIENT REQUIREMENTS:\n   • BOTH behaviors must be clear\n   • EACH must last ≥15% of plot\n   • Transitions must be identifiable\n\nCLASSIFICATION DECISION:\n\n1. One behavior ≥85%, other <10% → dominant class\n2. Both behaviors ≥15% → transient\n3. Minor behavior 10-15% → controversial\n4. Uncertain classification → controversial\n\nSUBTYPE GUIDELINES:\n• Be specific but accurate\n• For libration: \"sinusoidal\", \"apocentric\", \"noisy\", \"high-amplitude\"\n• For circulation: \"chaotic\", \"diagonal lines\", \"full scatter\"\n• For transient: describe sequence (e.g., \"libration then circulation\")\n• Don't default to \"apocentric\" unless TWO bands visible\n\nOutput format – exactly this JSON schema, nothing else:\n{\n  \"status\": \"<resonant | non-resonant | transient | controversial>\",\n  \"subtype\": \"<lower-case descriptive phrase>\"\n}\n\nBegin."

# PROMPT_TEMPLATE="Your custom prompt template here..."
